                <pb facs="0527" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/26805: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vera Cruz</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-19T19:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 19,
                                1924—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 21—12:44
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s January 15, 5 p.m., January 15, 7 p.m., January 16, noon.<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d337-f1"/> Following vigorous representations made to Mr. de
                    la Huerta in accordance with instructions, the Department of Marine informed me
                    that the terms of the blockade decree will not go into effect until the end of
                    the month.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
